            <ArticleTitle>Direct Evidence of Dirac Signature in Bilayer Germanene Islands on Cu(111).</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/adma.201606046</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bernal-stacked bilayer germanene with a stable buckled honeycomb structure has been successfully synthesized on Cu(111). Structural and electronic characterizations as well as theoretical calculations unequivocally demonstrate for the first time the presence of a nearly linear energy dispersion in the vicinity of the Fermi energy, as expected of the Dirac signature for theoretical freestanding germanene.</AbstractText>
